{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DEgp4JqeC541AynEKihSvL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Intervals.icu OAuth API scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR:WRITE authorize\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\"},{\"title\":\"Überauth intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090.md\"},{\"title\":\"open api\",\"url\":\"https://www.intervals.icu/features/open-api/\"},{\"title\":\"intervals icu tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\"},{\"title\":\"# API: Which fields contain birth\\\\_date, weight, and resting\\\\_hr in /athlete/{id} endpoint?\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-which-fields-contain-birth-date-weight-and-resting-hr-in-athlete-id-endpoint/127226/2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu API\",\"url\":\"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/\"},{\"title\":\"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io\",\"url\":\"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/latest/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html\"}]\n\nThe results confirm the scope format and what these three scopes cover, but I didn't find the authorize-page text itself.\n\n- **Format:** Scopes are a category plus READ or WRITE, joined with commas rather than spaces. For each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access). So `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` is a valid form.\n- **ACTIVITY:** covers completed rides, runs and similar activities.\n- **WELLNESS:** covers data such as weight and resting HR.\n- **CALENDAR:** covers planned workouts. Per a third-party Ueberauth wrapper, it also covers planned workouts and calendar events.\n- **Per-request override:** According to the same wrapper, scopes can be requested per authorization request, for example with a `scope=CALENDAR:WRITE` parameter.\n- **Tokens:** The same wrapper says there is no refresh token and no expiry. Treat this as unverified against Intervals.icu's own documentation.\n\nSources: the official Intervals.icu OAuth forum thread (forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759), the Ueberauth intervals.icu package docs on hex.pm, and the Intervals.icu API integration cookbook. Only the forum thread and cookbook are from Intervals.icu itself. I did not find the authorize-screen wording or the official API docs' scope table.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27cc2895-926f-4aac-974a-5a98998b128d","uuid":"4958a970-0eff-4274-ba3d-dd6a92812a43","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:31:08.776Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Intervals.icu OAuth API scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR:WRITE authorize","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DGDpVy8chinMTgoB8NZ23q","content":[{"title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},{"title":"Überauth intervals.icu","url":"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0"},{"title":"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090.md"},{"title":"open api","url":"https://www.intervals.icu/features/open-api/"},{"title":"intervals icu tools","url":"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools"},{"title":"# API: Which fields contain birth\\_date, weight, and resting\\_hr in /athlete/{id} endpoint?","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-which-fields-contain-birth-date-weight-and-resting-hr-in-athlete-id-endpoint/127226/2.md"},{"title":"Intervals.icu API","url":"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/"},{"title":"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io","url":"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/latest/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html"}]},"The results confirm the scope format and what these three scopes cover, but I didn't find the authorize-page text itself.\n\n- **Format:** Scopes are a category plus READ or WRITE, joined with commas rather than spaces. For each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access). So `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` is a valid form.\n- **ACTIVITY:** covers completed rides, runs and similar activities.\n- **WELLNESS:** covers data such as weight and resting HR.\n- **CALENDAR:** covers planned workouts. Per a third-party Ueberauth wrapper, it also covers planned workouts and calendar events.\n- **Per-request override:** According to the same wrapper, scopes can be requested per authorization request, for example with a `scope=CALENDAR:WRITE` parameter.\n- **Tokens:** The same wrapper says there is no refresh token and no expiry. Treat this as unverified against Intervals.icu's own documentation.\n\nSources: the official Intervals.icu OAuth forum thread (forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759), the Ueberauth intervals.icu package docs on hex.pm, and the Intervals.icu API integration cookbook. Only the forum thread and cookbook are from Intervals.icu itself. I did not find the authorize-screen wording or the official API docs' scope table."],"durationSeconds":7.507772957999994,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DEgp4JqeC541AynEKihSvL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
